d1a1/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": false, "main_agent_searched": true, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "\n**Suggested fix, not applied:**\n1. Rename `\"rat\"` to `\"fee_rate\"` in `settings.json`. This alone gives `Total: 5.0`.\n2. Optionally, remove the `except KeyError: rate = 0` fallback in `main.py`, or make it raise. A missing key would then fail loudly instead of giving a wrong total.\n\nDo you want me to apply either change?\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: bash]\nAll three readers use the same key, so I'll fix the key in `settings.json`.\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\nYes, the setting is read in three places. I fixed the bug, and all three paths now work.\n\n**Where `fee_rate` is read:**\n\n| File:line | How it reads the key |\n|---|---|\n| `main.py:11` | `cfg[\"fee_rate\"]`, falling back to `0` on `KeyError` |\n| `billing/report.py:7` | `get_setting(\"fee_rate\")`, which exits with \"fee_rate is missing\" if the value is `None` |\n| `billing/export/csv_writer.py:8` | `settings.get(\"fee_\" + \"rate\")`, which exits with \"fee_rate is missing\" if the value is `None` |\n\n`app/config.py:10` loads `settings.json` into `SETTINGS`, and `app/config.py:15` provides `get_setting`. Both are plumbing rather than readers of this key.\n\nOther files only mention similar names, and none of them read the setting:\n- `billing/discount.py:5` has a local `archived_fee_rate`.\n- `billing/invoice.py:5` has a column-name string.\n- `billing/tax.py` has a local `fee_schedule`.\n- `billing/audit.py:4` builds `\"fee_code\" + n`.\n\n**Fix:** In `settings.json:2` I changed `\"rat\"` to `\"fee_rate\"`. One change fixes all three readers, because they share the same key.\n\n**Results after the fix:**\n- `python3 main.py` prints `Total: 5.0`.\n- `python3 -m billing.report` prints `Report fee: 0.5`.\n- `python3 -m billing.export.csv_writer` prints `CSV fee: 0.5`.\n\nBefore the fix, `report` and `csv_writer` both exited with \"fee_rate is missing\", and `main.py` printed `Total: 0`.\n\nI left the `except KeyError: rate = 0` fallback in `main.py` alone. It is what hid this bug, so you may want to remove it so a missing key fails loudly.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 4, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 128919, "requests_cache_write": 109841, "requests_cost_usd": 0.3407384, "requests_count": 20, "requests_input_uncached": 2092, "requests_output": 4906, "reread": true, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "opencode:trig-subagent-followup:claude-opus-5-5:trial18", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 129, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-17T02:40:50.742005+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 4, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 351.794, "t_checker_s": 0.292, "t_env_setup_s": 0.003, "task": "trig-subagent-followup", "task_calls": 2, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 6998, "tokens_cache_read": 128919, "tokens_cache_write": 109841, "tokens_fresh": 2678, "tokens_input_uncached": 2092, "tokens_main_cache_read": 94184, "tokens_main_cache_write": 66709, "tokens_main_calls": 9, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 20, "tokens_main_output": 2658, "tokens_output": 4906, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": 128919, "tokens_proxy_cache_write": 109841, "tokens_proxy_calls": 20, "tokens_proxy_input_uncached": 2092, "tokens_proxy_output": 4906, "tokens_proxy_reasoning": null, "tokens_reasoning": 0, "toolchain": {"ai": 